{"name":"Pale Lychee","hex":"#c4acb2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pale","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Light in color.","Having a pallor (a light color, especially due to sickness, shock, fright etc.)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn pale; to lose colour.","To become insignificant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pale"},{"term":"lychee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The Chinese tropical fruit tree Litchi chinensis, of the soapberry family.","That tree's bright red oval fruit with a single stone surrounded by a fleshy white aril."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lychee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lychee","blocks":[{"text":"Lychees are the fruit of the tree Litchi chinensis, the sole member of the genus Litchi, part of the soapberry family, Sapindaceae. They are edible, with a sweet, mildly tart flavor, and have a distinctive floral aroma often described as rose-like."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Litchi_chinensis_fruits.JPG/330px-Litchi_chinensis_fruits.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lychee","wikidata":"Q13182"},{"title":"Colorfulness","blocks":[{"text":"Colorfulness, chroma and saturation are attributes of perceived color relating to chromatic intensity. As defined formally by the International Commission on Illumination (CIE) they respectively describe three different aspects of chromatic intensity, but the terms are often used loosely and interchangeably in contexts where these aspects are not clearly distinguished. The precise meanings of the terms vary by what other functions they are dependent on."},{"items":["Colorfulness is the \"attribute of a visual perception according to which the perceived color of an area appears to be more or less chromatic \". The colorfulness evoked by an object depends not only on its spectral reflectance but also on the strength of the illumination, and increases with the latter unless the brightness is very high.","Chroma is the \"colorfulness of an area judged as a proportion of the brightness of a similarly illuminated area that appears white or highly transmitting\". As a result, chroma is mostly only dependent on the spectral properties, and as such is seen to describe the object color. It is how different from a grey of the same lightness such an object color appears to be.","Saturation is the \"colorfulness of an area judged in proportion to its brightness\", which in effect is the perceived freedom from whitishness of the light coming from the area. An object with a given spectral reflectance exhibits approximately constant saturation for all levels of illumination, unless the brightness is very high."]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Brightness_and_colorfulness.png/330px-Brightness_and_colorfulness.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colorfulness","wikidata":"Q27673"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Sonnerat_litchi.jpg/330px-Sonnerat_litchi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Sonnerat_litchi.jpg/330px-Sonnerat_litchi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pierre Sonnerat's drawing from Voyage aux Indes Orientales et à la Chine (1782)[8]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASonnerat_litchi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg/500px-Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg/1280px-Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg/500px-Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Whole and opened fruit with seed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Lici Fruit Tree\" in Michał Boym's Flora Sinensis (1657)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlora_Sinensis_1656_(2950635)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Litchi_root.jpg/500px-Litchi_root.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Litchi_root.jpg/500px-Litchi_root.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Germinating lychee seed with its main root (about 3 months old)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALitchi_root.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a9/Lychee_seed.jpg/500px-Lychee_seed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a9/Lychee_seed.jpg/500px-Lychee_seed.jpg?utm_